    {
      "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-1-sec-36b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36B Complaints relating to the data sharing scheme",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022#sch-1-sec-36b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a complaint relates to the data sharing scheme within the\nmeaning of the Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022, the\nCommissioner may share information and documents about the\ncomplaint with the National Data Commissioner (the NDC), for the\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act\nNo. 12, 2022\n\npurposes of the NDC exercising powers, or performing functions\nor duties, under that Act.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may share only information and documents\nunder subsection (1) that were acquired by the Commissioner in\nthe course of exercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder this Act.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with the NDC under this section whether or not the\nCommissioner is transferring the complaint or part of the\ncomplaint to the NDC.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may transfer the complaint to the NDC under\nsection 50, if the Commissioner is of the opinion that the complaint\ncould have been made to the NDC.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a complaint relates to the data sharing scheme within the\nmeaning of the Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022, the\nCommissioner may share information and documents about the\ncomplaint with the National Data Commissioner (the NDC), for the\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act\nNo. 12, 2022\n\npurposes of the NDC exercising powers, or performing functions\nor duties, under that Act.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may share only information and documents\nunder subsection (1) that were acquired by the Commissioner in\nthe course of exercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder this Act.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with the NDC under this section whether or not the\nCommissioner is transferring the complaint or part of the\ncomplaint to the NDC.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may transfer the complaint to the NDC under\nsection 50, if the Commissioner is of the opinion that the complaint\ncould have been made to the NDC.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2345076ff3a2e8c7a7b376a873369c67fc4f992a1f2d4d88c59ee9229cf7840d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022#sch-1-sec-36b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36B Complaints relating to the data sharing scheme",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a complaint relates to the data sharing scheme within the\nmeaning of the Data Availability and Transparency Act 2022, the\nCommissioner may share information and documents about the\ncomplaint with the National Data Commissioner (the NDC), for the\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act\nNo. 12, 2022\n\npurposes of the NDC exercising powers, or performing functions\nor duties, under that Act.\n\n(2) The Commissioner may share only information and documents\nunder subsection (1) that were acquired by the Commissioner in\nthe course of exercising powers, or performing functions or duties,\nunder this Act.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, the Commissioner may share information or\ndocuments with the NDC under this section whether or not the\nCommissioner is transferring the complaint or part of the\ncomplaint to the NDC.\nNote:\nThe Commissioner may transfer the complaint to the NDC under\nsection 50, if the Commissioner is of the opinion that the complaint\ncould have been made to the NDC."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-1-sec-36b-ss-1",
