    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-3-sec-1-logic-descriptionlogic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Class hierarchy definition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "None",
      "cml:conclusionText": "DAT Act and rules have the same meaning in this Schedule as they do in the DAT Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-3-sec-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "2 Transitional provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022#sch-3-sec-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of the data sharing scheme, a transitional entity is\ntaken, during its transition period, to be accredited as an ADSP under\nthe DAT Act.\n(2)\nThe rules may prescribe conditions of accreditation applicable to a\ntransitional entity. For the purposes of the data sharing scheme as it\napplies because of subitem (1), any such condition is taken to have been\nimposed by the Commissioner under section 78 of the DAT Act.\nNote:\nUnder section 78 of the DAT Act as it applies because of subitem (1), the\nCommissioner may vary or remove a condition prescribed by the rules, or impose other\nconditions.\n(3)\nThe transition period for a transitional entity must end no later than the\nearlier of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commissioner cancels the entity’s accreditation as an\nADSP under section 81 of the DAT Act—the day the\ncancellation takes effect;\n\n(b) the end of the period of 40 months beginning on the day this\nAct receives the Royal Assent.\n3  This Schedule is part of the data sharing scheme\nThe data sharing scheme is taken to include this Schedule and the rules.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 12, 2022\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nFor the purposes of the data sharing scheme, a transitional entity is\ntaken, during its transition period, to be accredited as an ADSP under\nthe DAT Act.\n(2)\nThe rules may prescribe conditions of accreditation applicable to a\ntransitional entity. For the purposes of the data sharing scheme as it\napplies because of subitem (1), any such condition is taken to have been\nimposed by the Commissioner under section 78 of the DAT Act.\nNote:\nUnder section 78 of the DAT Act as it applies because of subitem (1), the\nCommissioner may vary or remove a condition prescribed by the rules, or impose other\nconditions.\n(3)\nThe transition period for a transitional entity must end no later than the\nearlier of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commissioner cancels the entity’s accreditation as an\nADSP under section 81 of the DAT Act—the day the\ncancellation takes effect;\n\n(b) the end of the period of 40 months beginning on the day this\nAct receives the Royal Assent.\n3  This Schedule is part of the data sharing scheme\nThe data sharing scheme is taken to include this Schedule and the rules.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 12, 2022\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-3-sec-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022-sch-3-sec-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cf089df8b54179e41bd004de6f7770704706f699d7c3025bcef4a93bbdab5cf5",
      "skos:note": "A transitional entity is accredited as an ADSP under the DAT Act during its transition period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/data-availability-and-transparency-consequential-amendments-act-2022#sch-3-sec-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "2 Transitional provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nFor the purposes of the data sharing scheme, a transitional entity is\ntaken, during its transition period, to be accredited as an ADSP under\nthe DAT Act.\n(2)\nThe rules may prescribe conditions of accreditation applicable to a\ntransitional entity. For the purposes of the data sharing scheme as it\napplies because of subitem (1), any such condition is taken to have been\nimposed by the Commissioner under section 78 of the DAT Act.\nNote:\nUnder section 78 of the DAT Act as it applies because of subitem (1), the\nCommissioner may vary or remove a condition prescribed by the rules, or impose other\nconditions.\n(3)\nThe transition period for a transitional entity must end no later than the\nearlier of the following:\n\n(a) if the Commissioner cancels the entity’s accreditation as an\nADSP under section 81 of the DAT Act—the day the\ncancellation takes effect;\n\n(b) the end of the period of 40 months beginning on the day this\nAct receives the Royal Assent.\n3  This Schedule is part of the data sharing scheme\nThe data sharing scheme is taken to include this Schedule and the rules.\n\nTransitional provisions  Schedule 3\n\nNo. 12, 2022\nData Availability and Transparency (Consequential Amendments) Act"
    },
